Compare three properties with one concrete example each. Need maybe use same scenario? User says using one concrete example for each. Could use examples:
- Read-after-write consistency: client writes x=1, then reads x from same client/session; must see 1. Example: user updates profile name, immediately reloads profile; if sees old name violates. But if read from different client? not required.
- Monotonic reads: same client reads x=1, later reads x; must not see older value (e.g., 0) after seeing 1. Example: client reads counter 5, then 4 due to replica lag/cache; violates.
- Linearizability: all operations appear to occur atomically at some point between invocation and response, in real-time order. Example: two clients write/read concurrently: C1 writes x=1 at t1, C2 reads x at t2 after C1's write response? Need linearizability requires if write completes before read starts, read sees 1. Concrete: C1 writes
